            "review_title": "Review at Hakata Ineya Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Tài V\n8 contributions\n0\nSashimi cut pretty hard.\nMar 2026 • Business\n- 99k soybeans cooked, this dish is delicious but it is silly =)) This soybeans is as soft as the house does, eating sugar soybeans is so soft. Light fat, eating vs saltwater, ponzu, chicken fever vs salt\n- Sashimi 3 kinds of 259k, sashimi here cut thick vl too, thickest we have ever eaten @.@ any fish is fresh, fine tuna too. Feel like one piece of fish here = 1.5 pieces elsewhere.\n- 219k grilled orange, bone fish, which is deliciously baked. I don’t know why the kitchen is so juicy.\n- 139k orange stock, thick stock fish, a little sweet, I see eating okela and eating rice is a little pale. And the fish here are fine, none of them are dried, but this stock fish, and the oranges are x2 degrees dry.\n- Crusher rice 189k, just 2 cups of rice, cooked at the table too. Nice, there's nothing to feed, inside there's chicken, vegetables vs. what else I forgot...\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten March 28, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
